  "body": "``` js\ncreateImageBitmap(svgBlob, 0, 0, 10, 10, {\n  resizeWidth: 100,\n  resizeHeight: 100\n});\n```\n\nIdeally the UA should be able to perform cropping & resizing prior to rasterization. This has a performance benefit as the UA doesn't need to rasterize parts of the image that will be discarded during cropping, and will ensure the output is sharp.\n\nThere isn't currently a way to set the viewport width/height when it comes to rasterization, which impacts things like media queries within SVG. These are often different to the output pixel width/height, as the output pixel width is often multiplied by the device pixel ratio, whereas the viewport width isn't.\n\nCurrently https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#cropped-to-the-source-rectangle-with-formatting takes bitmap data, suggesting rasterization has already occured, which breaks the expectations above.\n\n+@junov \n",
